Ey up! Reet way t' solve this is t' count maximal non-decreasin' runs o' letters. Fer each contiguous run o' length L, every substring wholly inside it is sorted, an' there're L*(L+1)/2 o' them. Sum that over all runs.

Algorithm:
- Read T.
- For each test: read N an' S.
- Walk S left t' right, keep cur=1 fer current non-decreasin' run.
- For i from 1 t' N-1: if S[i-1] <= S[i] then cur++ else add cur*(cur+1)/2 t' ans an' cur=1.
- After loop add last run's cur*(cur+1)/2 an' print ans (use 64-bit integer).

Complexity: O(N) time, O(1) extra space. Use long long t' avoid overflow.

Example C++ implementaion:

#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int T; if(!(cin>>T)) return 0;
    while(T--){
        int N; string S; cin>>N>>S;
        long long ans = 0;
        long long cur = 1;
        for(int i = 1; i < N; ++i){
            if(S[i-1] <= S[i]) cur++;
            else { ans += cur*(cur+1)/2; cur = 1; }
        }
        ans += cur*(cur+1)/2;
        cout << ans << '\n';
    }
}

